    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$15,\\ 420$ or $60,\\ 105$.",
      "worked": "Write the numbers as $a=15x$ and $b=15y$, where $x$ and $y$ are coprime.\n$$\\begin{align*}ab&=15\\times420\\\\225xy&=6300\\\\xy&=28\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor pairs of $28$ are $(1,28)$, $(2,14)$ and $(4,7)$. Only $(1,28)$ and $(4,7)$ are coprime.\n$$\\begin{align*}(a,b)&=(15\\times1,15\\times28)\\\\(a,b)&=(15,420)\\\\(a,b)&=(15\\times4,15\\times7)\\\\(a,b)&=(60,105)\\end{align*}$$\nBoth pairs have HCF $15$ and LCM $420$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
